Fun fact:  16th Avenue refers to Nashville's Music Row.

TIP:  The opening step down also repeats twice more in the song and is easy to play.  Notes may or may not transpose.  Untransposed, it's just top string/2nd fret <g>, top string/1st fret <f#>, and top string open <e>.  In the body of the song it will come after a (G).  


